	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "TE Connectivity DEUTSCH DT13-4P, sealed automotive PCB header receptacle, 4 positions, RIGHT ANGLE (90deg) molded pins, FLANGED front panel mount; DEUTSCH size 16 contacts, 13 A on 14-16 AWG / 10 A on 18 AWG / 7.5 A on 20 AWG, 250 VAC/VDC, -55..+125 degC, 100 mating cycles, 20 G / 10-2000 Hz per 108-151009 rev E (22AUG2024); that spec rates IP68/IP6K9K for the INLINE plug+receptacle with rear protection only - headers and flanged versions are listed Not Tested. Mates with DT06-4S-XXXX plug + W4S wedge lock. Geometry from TE customer drawing DT13-4P rev C1 (03JUL2014) + application spec 114-151046 rev A (28AUG2020) sec.3.4, cross-checked against TE STEP model C-DT13-4P (2017-01-24), agreement 0.001 mm. PCB layout: 4x finished hole D1.88 +/-0.05 (pin D1.5748), pin pitch 4.445 x 6.35 mm; 3x NPTH D3.43 +0.12/-0.00 for #4-20 Plastite 48 thread-forming screws, pair 17.2974 mm apart, third hole 11.430 mm toward the panel on the pair axis midpoint. Mating axis sits 17.856 mm above the PCB top surface; pins protrude 3.10 +/-0.64 below it. Panel inner face (seal land) is 22.479 mm from the pin-1 row (Dwgs.User line); overall body 38.354 (X) x 39.507 (Y), the shroud protrudes 13.97 mm in front of the panel; cutout centre at X=+0.6858, 17.856 mm above the PCB top. Panel cutout option 2: 20.73 (screw axis) x 21.84 mm, 4x R6.35, plus 2x D3.94 for #6-19 screws on the screw axis 28.448 mm apart; panel 6.25 mm max. CAVEAT: application-spec fig. 3.4 is drawn as seen from the connector underside; this footprint follows the STEP model and the mating-face view, so pin 1 is the rear row on the -X side. If the fab NPTH tolerance is negative, order the mounting holes at 3.45-3.50 (spec allows 3.43 to 3.55). https://www.te.com/en/product-DT13-4P.html")
	(tags "connector DEUTSCH DT DT13 4 pin position right angle 90deg flange panel mount sealed automotive TE size 16 13A IP67 header receptacle")
